If $S: V -> W$ has matrix representation $matbold(N)$ with respect to the same bases, then for scalars $alpha, beta$ the map $alpha T + beta S$ is represented by the matrix $alpha matbold(M) + beta matbold(N)$ with coefficients
$ (alpha matbold(M) + beta matbold(N))_(i j) = alpha M_(i j) + beta N_(i j), $
because addition and scalar multiplication of matrices take place entry-wise.
